      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 896,
        "content": "## WooCommerce Products -Pinecone - EN\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow synchronizes WooCommerce products into a Pinecone vector index for search or retrieval use cases. It can run manually or on a schedule, loads the current WooCommerce catalog, compares it with a local deduplication table, removes vectors for deleted products, and processes active products in batches. For each product, it enriches variable products with variations and reviews, formats the product text, replaces old Pinecone chunks, stores new vector documents, and records the sync state.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure WooCommerce API access in the HTTP Request nodes, including the store base URL and any required consumer key/secret authentication.\n- Update the \u201eSet API Settings\u201d node with wooBaseUrl, wooCurrency, pineconeIndexName, and pineconeIndexHost for your environment.\n- Configure Pinecone credentials and ensure the target index exists and matches the embedding model dimensions.\n- Configure OpenAI credentials for the product embedding node.\n- Create or verify the n8n Data Table used for product sync/dedup entries, including fields needed to track product IDs and sync metadata.\n- Review the schedule trigger timing and enable it when automatic product synchronization is desired.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust batch selection logic, product formatting code, text splitter settings, embedding model, Pinecone namespace/index, or the fields included from WooCommerce products, variations, and reviews."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "5ac703ff-99da-4bb3-af48-351f34566c35",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
